        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Katsue wrote:</b><br><blockquote>To avoid needless asymmetry. It makes no sense to me to say that a power hasn't been used until it's been resolved, while a card has been played even though it hasn't resolved.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nOne-Shot \"A keyword appearing on hero and villain cards. The effects of a one-shots happen immediately upon being played.\"That roughly translates to \"when this card is played, do x\". This brings us to the triggers of \"when a card is played, do x\" so order of play now takes effect. Considering any card that has this trigger that is already in play would have to of been in play prior to this new card entering play, as cards can't enter play at the same time.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That answers my edit question above. I buy that.&nbsp;</p>",
