      {
        "id": 71447,
        "name": "Katsue",
        "username": "Katsue",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/{size}/2012_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-26T22:21:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hairtrigger seems dependent on just a target entering play (how does that shut matriarch down? Auto shredding fowls isn't exactly the best strat without meta gaming)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'd assume that a card entering play is the first step of a card play. And it would shut The Matriarch down by killing the Fowl, thus preventing the Fowl's \"play another card\" text from activating before it even happens. Effectively it would act as a permanent semi-Take Down.</p>",
