      {
        "id": 71449,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-26T22:28:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p>A card entering play is what causes a card's effect to take place. &nbsp;Therefore any other effect that also triggers on a card entering play would happen simultaneously with the effect of the card, and since that would be resolved in the order the cards came into play, the new card is at the back of the line.</p></blockquote><p>That makes sense to me.&nbsp; I still haven't seen anything official on the subject, but if this were the official ruling, I'd be able to understand it better than cards and their text entering play at different points in time.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
