      {
        "id": 71452,
        "name": "quiksterboy44",
        "username": "quiksterboy44",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/quiksterboy44/{size}/2480_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-26T22:52:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A card entering play is what causes a card's effect to take place.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I can understand this, I always thought a card being played is what causes the text effect to go off regardless of when it's counted as \"entered play\". I guess I never really thought about what the phrase \"entering play\" actually meant, like entering the playfield or entering card order que, somewhere along those lines.</p>\n<p>good point phantaskippy</p>",
